    "report_excerpt": "I found two real domain availability API services:\n\n**1. WhoisXML API - Domain Availability API**\n- URL: https://www.whoisxmlapi.com/\n- Features: 1.2 billion+ domains tracked, 7,596+ TLDs supported\n- Free tier: 100 API credits (no credit card required)\n- Checks if domains can be purchased for domainers or companies expanding online portfolios\n\n**2. GoDaddy API - Domain Availability Check**\n- URL: https://developer.godaddy.com/\n- Endpoint: GET /v3/domains/check-availability\n- Requires a Personal Access Token (PAT)\n- Returns availability status plus current pricing for registration terms\n- API docs: https://developer.godaddy.com/en/docs/api-users/quickstart\n\nBoth are legitimate services for checking whether domain names are available to register. WhoisXML is more focused on intelligence/security, while GoDaddy's API is specifically for domain registration availability and pricing.",
